    {
      "page_title": "Month-to-Date Totals and Quick Picks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Month-to-date total",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT ts, amt, SUM(amt) OVER (",
            "  PARTITION BY",
            "    date_trunc('month', ts)",
            "  ORDER BY ts, id",
            "  ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING) mtd",
            "FROM sales;"
          ],
          "note": "resets on the first of each month"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`PARTITION BY` accepts **expressions**, not just columns",
            "One window per month, so the total restarts itself",
            "Add `region` to the list for one window per pair"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. ORDER BY changes meaning",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "OVER clause",
            "Frame",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(PARTITION BY g)",
              "whole partition",
              "group total"
            ],
            [
              "(PARTITION BY g ORDER BY d)",
              "start..current",
              "running total"
            ],
            [
              "(ORDER BY d)",
              "start..current",
              "global running"
            ],
            [
              "()",
              "whole result",
              "grand total"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : amount / SUM(amount) OVER () * 100 gives each row's percent of total.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Outer ORDER BY",
          "text": "The ORDER BY inside OVER does not sort output. Add a final ORDER BY."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Quick pick",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Write"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Balance so far",
              "SUM + ROWS UNBOUNDED"
            ],
            [
              "Last 3 rows",
              "AVG + 2 PRECEDING"
            ],
            [
              "Last 7 days",
              "AVG + RANGE INTERVAL"
            ],
            [
              "Share of total",
              "SUM(x) OVER ()"
            ],
            [
              "Rows so far",
              "COUNT(*) + ROWS"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assuming rows come back in window order",
            "Adding ORDER BY and not noticing the frame changed",
            "Forgetting `PARTITION BY` so accounts blend together"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pre-flight checklist",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use **ROWS** when you want one step per row",
            "Add a unique tiebreaker to ORDER BY",
            "Use ==RANGE== only for calendar-true windows",
            "Mask the first N-1 rows of a moving average",
            "Add `PARTITION BY` when data holds many entities"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "The default frame is RANGE, so write ROWS yourself whenever you want one step per row."
        }
      ],
