    {
      "page_title": "FIRST, LAST and NTH_VALUE Frames",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What they return",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==FIRST_VALUE(x)== gives x from the first row of the frame",
            "==LAST_VALUE(x)== gives x from the last row of the frame",
            "==NTH_VALUE(x, n)== gives the nth frame row, NULL if frame is smaller",
            "==NTILE(n)== splits an ordered partition into n buckets, 1..n"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT day, price,",
            "FIRST_VALUE(price) OVER w AS launch,",
            "price - FIRST_VALUE(price) OVER w",
            "FROM prices",
            "WINDOW w AS (PARTITION BY product",
            "  ORDER BY day);"
          ],
          "note": "Every price vs the launch price"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**LAST_VALUE** with default frame returns the row's own value",
            "Default frame ends at `CURRENT ROW`, so no row is ever \"later\"",
            "NTH_VALUE has the same trap: second highest needs the full frame",
            "`IGNORE NULLS` needs PostgreSQL 19+; `FROM LAST` is unsupported"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Why it breaks",
          "text": "With ORDER BY, the frame is start → current row. The last row of that frame is always you."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Fixing the frame",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "LAST_VALUE(price) OVER (",
            "PARTITION BY product ORDER BY day",
            "ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING",
            "AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING) AS last"
          ],
          "note": "Full frame, or LAST_VALUE lies"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Trick",
            "Frame needed"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Last value",
              "{green:fix} full frame",
              "UNBOUNDED both"
            ],
            [
              "Last value",
              "FIRST_VALUE + `DESC`",
              "default is fine"
            ],
            [
              "2nd highest",
              "NTH_VALUE(x, 2) DESC",
              "UNBOUNDED both"
            ],
            [
              "Skip NULLs",
              "running-count groups",
              "n/a"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: 10 rows, NTILE(4)",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
