    {
      "page_title": "Filtering Window Results with Subqueries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why WHERE Fails",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`WHERE` cannot reference a ==window function==: windows run **after** WHERE",
            "Order: FROM → WHERE → GROUP BY → HAVING → window → SELECT",
            "PostgreSQL has no `QUALIFY` (Snowflake, BigQuery, Teradata do)",
            "So wrap the window, then filter the outer query"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Four Patterns",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Best for",
            "Shape"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Subquery",
              "one row per group",
              "rn = 1"
            ],
            [
              "CTE",
              "top N with ties",
              "rk <= 3"
            ],
            [
              "DISTINCT ON",
              "latest per key",
              "PG only"
            ],
            [
              "LATERAL",
              "few groups, big table",
              "LIMIT 3"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT * FROM (",
            "  SELECT *, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (",
            "    PARTITION BY user_id",
            "    ORDER BY ts DESC) rn",
            "  FROM t) s WHERE rn = 1;"
          ],
          "note": "Pattern 1: subquery, filter outside"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "WITH r AS (",
            "  SELECT *, RANK() OVER (",
            "    ORDER BY score DESC) rk",
            "  FROM t)",
            "SELECT * FROM r WHERE rk <= 3;"
          ],
          "note": "Pattern 2: CTE, RANK keeps ties"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. PG-Native Shortcuts",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT DISTINCT ON (user_id) *",
            "FROM t",
            "ORDER BY user_id, ts DESC;",
            "-- latest row per user"
          ],
          "note": "ORDER BY must start with ON cols"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==DISTINCT ON== is PostgreSQL specific and concise",
            "Often faster than `ROW_NUMBER` for one row per group",
            "No rank column to drop afterwards"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "FROM users u, LATERAL (",
            "  SELECT * FROM orders o",
            "  WHERE o.uid = u.id",
            "  ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT 3",
            ") top3"
          ],
          "note": "Pattern 4: needs index (uid, ts)"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "LATERAL wins when",
          "text": "few groups are needed from many rows: with an index it beats a full window scan."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Before vs After",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Filter placed",
            "Window sees",
            "Rank is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Inside subquery",
              "only kept rows",
              "relative to subset"
            ],
            [
              "Outside (after)",
              "all rows",
              "global"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "Compute the window first, filter one level up: subquery, CTE, DISTINCT ON or LATERAL."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "postgresql",
      "subtitle": "QUALIFY alternatives"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Filtering Pitfalls and Aggregate Windows",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Filter inside the subquery when you wanted rank over **all** rows",
            "`HAVING SUM(x) OVER ()` is always invalid: windows run after HAVING",
            "Using `WHERE rn = 1` in the same SELECT as the window"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT dept, SUM(x),",
            "  RANK() OVER (",
            "    ORDER BY SUM(x) DESC)",
            "FROM t GROUP BY dept;"
          ],
          "note": "Window over aggregates: group first"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "postgresql",
      "subtitle": "QUALIFY alternatives"
    },
